<%#
  Why this claim has no AI verdict and never will: the submitter's consent
  doesn't cover the check. Shared by the Review card (_ai_verdict) and the
  finance edit page, so both read identically. Local: expense.

  Deliberately neutral: plain grey text, no alert box, no badge. A submitter who
  declined has done nothing wrong, and this must not read as a failed, errored or
  flagged check — it is simply a claim finance checks the way they did before the
  checker existed. There is no override: a refusal is final.
%>
<p class="mb-0 text-sm text-gray-600">
  <span class="font-medium">Not checked.</span>
  <% if expense.ai_processing_declined? %>
    The submitter did not consent to AI processing, so the receipt was never sent to Google.
  <% else %>
    There is no consent to AI processing recorded for this claim, so the receipt was never sent
    to Google. Claims submitted before we started asking, and claims that arrive by email, were
    never asked.
  <% end %>
  Please check it against the receipt yourself.
</p>
